# --- the daily digest (ADR-0033) ---
# 09:00 -- ONE markdown message to nas-infra, replacing every routine push the
# six-lane split deliberately stopped sending: successful cron runs, */5 sweeps
# that changed nothing, enforcer runs with no drift. It reports STATE, not
# events, so a digest that arrives late is still correct.
#
# It also reports how many notifications the cooldowns swallowed. That number is
# what keeps the whole scheme honest: zero every day means the windows are too
# short to be doing anything, and a huge number means something is flapping.
# Without it, "quiet" and "broken" are indistinguishable from a phone.
#
# --ok-codes 0,1 (the default) is right here: exit 1 means a section could not
# be collected, which is a gap in the digest and not a failed job.
